<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 309 0 R/Pg 64 0 R/A[2198 0 R 0]/K[24]>>
endobj

1265 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 309 0 R/Pg 64 0 R/A[2199 0 R 0]/K[25]>>
endobj

1266 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(gratitude guaranteed that life would give me what I wanted, but because it loosened adversity's grip on my mind. It was a kind of alchemy: it could transform the way I experienced adversity, even when it could not transform the circumstances themselves.)/Pg 65 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

1267 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(Honesty became non-negotiable for me. Why? Because I began to recognise that listening inwardly required distinguishing genuine conscience from the familiar voices of fear, vanity, self-interest and the desire to impress others.)/Pg 65 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

1268 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(For years, I had adjusted myself to external expectations, manipulated situations for personal advantage and sought approval. Somewhere along the way, I had lost touch with a quieter voice that did not need applause.)/Pg 65 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

1269 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(I came to regard that voice as my higher self, my conscience or, in my personal understanding, God. I was determined not to lose touch with it again.)/Pg 65 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

1270 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(I cannot claim that every inner voice is divine, or that every feeling of certainty should be trusted. My commitment was to cultivate the honesty to examine my motives rather than automatically believe whatever my mind told me.)/Pg 65 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

1271 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 310 0 R/T(6. When Gratitude Met Physical Pain)/E(6. When Gratitude Met Physical Pain)/Pg 65 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

1272 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(This may sound far-fetched, but I will not omit what I experienced simply because it sounds unusual.)/Pg 65 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

1273 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(Two incidents left a lasting impression on me, both involving some of the most )/Pg 65 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

1274 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 310 0 R/T(excruciating physical pain I had known. In the first, the fingers of my left hand were crushed by a sudden jolt.)/E(excruciating physical pain I had known. In the first, the fingers of my left hand were crushed by a sudden jolt.)/Pg 65 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

1275 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(In the second, I unexpectedly fell to the floor, landing on both elbows.)/Pg 65 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

1276 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(I do not know exactly what happened within me in those moments. But on both occasions, my first spontaneous words were:)/Pg 65 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

1277 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E("Thank you, God.")/Pg 65 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

1278 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(And, to my astonishment, the pain seemed to disappear almost instantly. The tingling around the affected areas continued for some time, but the acute pain was no longer present in the same way.)/Pg 65 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

1279 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(Did gratitude alter my perception of pain? Was there another explanation? I cannot say with certainty. I would not claim that gratitude medically eliminates pain or replaces appropriate treatment for an injury. But I cannot deny what I experienced.)/Pg 65 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

1280 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(The same principle seemed to help during intense humiliation and psychological suffering. When I remembered to express gratitude, the distress often began to subside. It was not mere resignation; it felt like a transformation in my relationship with the event itself. Instead of asking, "Why is this happening to me?", I began responding, "Thank you, God.")/Pg 65 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

1281 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E(To an ordinary observer, this might sound irrational. Why thank God for suffering? Why not protest or demand an explanation? I would once have )/Pg 65 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

1282 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 310 0 R/E<FEFF092E09410915094D0924093F092C094B0927002D002000350034>/Pg 65 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

1283 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(asked precisely the same questions.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

1284 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(But I began to see that gratitude was not an endorsement of injustice or a declaration that suffering was desirable. It was a way of refusing to let suffering dictate my entire inner experience. And yes, I sometimes treated adversity itself as a form of divine grace\204not because I could prove that every painful event had been sent for my benefit, but because I could choose to meet it in a way that fostered awareness rather than bitterness.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

1285 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(To some, I may have appeared crazy. But I began to wonder whether being considered crazy was preferable to remaining trapped in patterns that repeatedly made me miserable. After all, what is the greater folly: questioning your habitual interpretation of life, or unquestioningly allowing it to govern you?)/Pg 66 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

1286 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 311 0 R/T(7. My First Realisation: God as a Verb)/E(7. My First Realisation: God as a Verb)/Pg 66 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

1287 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(Eventually, I arrived at a conclusion that would once have sounded absurd to my former atheist self.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

1288 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(I had spent years debating whether God existed as a being, a person or a supreme entity. But my own experience was leading me towards a different understanding. Whenever something helped me move from turmoil towards clarity, from suffering towards solace, or from self-defeating patterns towards a more honest way of living, I experienced it as an expression of what I called God.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

1289 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(And then the idea struck me:)/Pg 66 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

1290 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(My journey had begun with a desperate demand:)/Pg 66 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

1291 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E("Somebody out there, please save me from myself!")/Pg 66 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

1292 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(It had progressed through surrender, listening and gratitude. And now I was beginning to understand that the help I had sought might not arrive as a supernatural intervention. It could emerge through a counsellor's words, a colleague's uncomfortable advice, or a moment of awareness that interrupted my habitual suffering.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

1293 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(Perhaps the divine, if that is what one chooses to call it, need not always arrive with a halo and a heavenly announcement.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

1294 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(Sometimes, it arrives disguised as a psychologist who does not believe in God.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

1295 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(Sometimes, as a colleague who refuses to sympathise with your self-pity.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

1296 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(And sometimes, as a handkerchief you had never previously considered worth thanking anyone for.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

1297 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(Perhaps, as I now understand it, God is not merely a noun.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

1298 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(God is a verb.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

1299 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(Not merely something to worship, praise or petition\204but something I experience through the movement from confusion towards clarity, from resentment towards gratitude, and from self-deception towards honesty.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

1300 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E(This did not prove that God was a supernatural entity. It gave me a different way of understanding what I had been seeking.)/Pg 66 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

1301 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 311 0 R/E<FEFF092E09410915094D0924093F092C094B0927002D002000350035>/Pg 66 0 R/K[18]>>
